---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import Byline from "../components/Byline.astro";
import LegalNote from "../components/LegalNote.astro";
import { LINKS, CANON_PATHS, linkClass, ext } from "../lib/links";
import { withBase } from "../lib/base";

const path = "/retailbi-firearm-sales-index";
const crumbs = [
  { name: "Home", path: "/" },
  { name: "How to read the Index", path },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How to read a same-store print without getting hypnotized | FFL Intel"
  description="Gearfire’s monthly Firearm Sales Index is a register series. That is a real thing. It is still last month."
  path={path}
  ogImagePath={CANON_PATHS.tzu}
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-12 sm:py-14">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-sky-400 mb-3">
      The Index
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white text-balance mb-4">
      How to read a same-store print without getting hypnotized
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-zinc-300 mb-6">
      A monthly percent-change from a stable panel of stores is a tool. It is
      not the market speaking in a single voice.
    </p>
    <Byline dateLabel="August 13, 2026" read="6 min" />

    <figure class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800">
      <img
        src={withBase(`${CANON_PATHS.tzu}?v=2`)}
        alt="Betsy Tzu — Art of Demand"
        width="1280"
        height="720"
        class="w-full"
      />
      <figcaption class="px-4 py-2 text-[11px] text-zinc-500">
        Art of Demand — illustration, not a product shot.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.7] text-zinc-300 font-serif">
      <p>
        Public materials describe the RetailBI Firearm Sales Index as
        same-store adjusted new firearm unit sales, compiled from a selected
        subset of Gearfire-network retailers, then published as a monthly
        percent-change. That design tries to keep openings, closings, and
        partner churn from pretending to be demand.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you already sit in that dashboard, you know what it is good at:
        confirmed units, a panel, a closed window. You also know what it cannot
        be. It is not NICS. It is not used guns. It is not the sentence a
        shopper typed at 9:40 p.m.
      </p>
      <p>
        I print Index figures only with a date and a source. Last public one on
        this desk: March 2026, −11.9 percent year-over-year, Outdoor Wire, 13
        April 2026. As they reported it — not our number.
      </p>
      <p>
        After you read the print, the next honest question is still the ask.
        Side-by-side of those factories:{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.fortress} class={linkClass} {...ext}
          >RetailBI vs Betsy</a
        >
        {" · "}
        <a href={LINKS.gseIndex} class={linkClass} {...ext}>GSE Index spoke</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-10"><LegalNote fortress /></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
